{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791672427,"nonce":"D4F61NFjkXY/9JH3wx1RF57UZhk=","title":"A layout listener that wrote made the next listener's reads throw","message":"Layout.compute runs its onLaidOut listeners one after another and runs layout again for any that return true. A listener that wrote, to move or resize something, left the bounds unreadable until layout ran again, so the next listener's first read threw \"Compute layout before reading bounds\". Which pages hit it depended on the order the listeners were added in and on which of them had work.\n\nReproduced with the wiki's tabs page: the top layer, text fields and a tab indicator each have a listener; one that wrote broke the indicator's read.\n\nFix: the listeners after one that returned true wait for the next pass, in which all run again. Each finds its work again from the layout, which the three existing ones already do. tests/native-layout.mjs has a writer and a reader and requires the reader to wait.","files":null}]}